# THE SIFREI ROWS OF PISKAOT 222-226 (THE DEUTERONOMY WALK sitting 17 — CHAPTERS 22-25, LEAN, 2026-09-25): the distance of a ris, unloading and loading, the
# enemy's ox against the inclination, what is a lost object, the exemptions and the five returns (222 — HEADLESS, on 22:1, opening on Exodus 23:5; read whole
# from the export); far as near, not another house, the marks and the fraud, the lost man himself (223); the ass works and eats, the garment shaken every thirty
# days, the vessels used not worn, the garment's marks and claimants, less than a perutah (224); the fallen ass and its owner's part (225); the garments of the
# other sex, R. Eliezer b. Jacob's weapons, the five epithets (226). Every row READ WHOLE in both files (the whole-row rule); the cuts by ch22_ink.SP_ (the
# misses collected). Sitting 16's form.
from ch22_ink import *
S = {}
def srow(p, r, verdict, prose): S[(p, r)] = (verdict, prose)

srow(222, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"WHEN YOU SEE" (Exodus 23:5) — EVEN A FULL MIL AWAY? THE TEACHING SAYS "WHEN YOU ENCOUNTER" (Exodus 23:4); ENCOUNTER IN ITS PLAIN SENSE? "WHEN YOU SEE" — HOW? THE SAGES ESTIMATED ONE IN SEVEN AND A HALF OF A MIL, A RIS. The head row of the headless piska 222, opening on Exodus 23:5 and not on 22:1 ({SP_(222, 1, "שערו", "חכמים", "אחד", "משבעה", "ומחצה", "במיל")} "the Sages estimated one of seven and a half in a mil"; {SP_(222, 1, "שהוא", "ריס")} "which is a ris"): THE DISTANCE PARAMETER of the return\'s duty — the sighting within a ris (some 150 yards), between "see" and "encounter"; the answer sheet\'s own estimate (Tosefta Bava Metzia 2:25, not opened). The piska on the twin law read at the twin\'s verse — chapter 22\'s spine opens in Exodus. Fresh.')
srow(222, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOU REFRAIN FROM RELEASING — YOU SHALL SURELY RELEASE WITH HIM" (Exodus 23:5) — WE LEARN THAT HE TRANSGRESSES A POSITIVE AND A NEGATIVE COMMANDMENT. ({SP_(222, 2, "מצות", "עשה")} "a positive commandment"; {SP_(222, 2, "מצות", "לא", "תעשה")} "a negative commandment"): the two classes of the one duty — the compile\'s effect carries both (the refusal a prohibition broken, the release a command undone). Fresh.')
srow(222, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"RELEASE WITH HIM" — UNLOADING; "RAISE WITH HIM" (22:4) — LOADING: R. JUDAH B. BETHYRA. ({SP_(222, 3, "זו", "פריקה")} "this is unloading"; {SP_(222, 3, "זו", "טעינה")} "this is loading"): THE TWO DUTIES DISTINGUISHED — Exodus commands the unburdening, Deuteronomy the reloading; two effects of the fallen-beast cell (Bava Metzia 2:10 the answer sheet on the two). Fresh.')
srow(222, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"YOU SHALL NOT SEE YOUR BROTHER\'S OX" (22:1) — A NEGATIVE COMMANDMENT; ELSEWHERE "WHEN YOU ENCOUNTER" (Exodus 23:4) — A POSITIVE ONE. The first row citing chapter 22 ({SP_(222, 4, "מצות", "לא", "תעשה")} "a negative commandment"): the lost thing\'s duty a pair as the fallen beast\'s (222:2) — the Deuteronomy verse the prohibition, the Exodus verse the command. Fresh.')
srow(222, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"YOUR BROTHER\'S OX" — ONLY YOUR BROTHER\'S? YOUR ENEMY\'S FROM "YOUR ENEMY" (Exodus 23:4) — ANY OWNER; WHY "BROTHER"? THE TORAH SPEAKS ONLY AGAINST THE INCLINATION. ({SP_(222, 5, "שור", "אויבך", "מנין")} "your enemy\'s ox — whence?"; {SP_(222, 5, "כנגד", "היצר")} "against the inclination"): THE SCOPE every owner, brother or enemy — and the reason the word "brother" stands: the law addresses the inclination, not the class (225:2 the same words for the ass). Fresh.')
srow(222, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'"OR HIS SHEEP STRAYING" — IN THE MANNER OF THEIR STRAYING; HENCE (BAVA METZIA 2:9): WHAT IS A LOST OBJECT? AN ASS OR A COW GRAZING ON THE ROAD — NOT LOST; AN ASS WITH ITS GEAR OVERTURNED, A COW RUNNING AMONG THE VINEYARDS — LOST. THE MISHNAH CITED IN THE HEBREW BY NAME ({SP_(222, 6, "איזו", "היא", "אבדה")} "what is a lost object?"; {SP_(222, 6, "חמור", "וכליו", "הפוכים")} "an ass with its gear overturned"): THE PREDICATE "lost" defined by the beast\'s manner — the compile\'s condition on the duty (the answer sheet inside the spine). Fresh.')
srow(222, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOU HIDE YOURSELF FROM THEM" — SOMETIMES YOU HIDE AND SOMETIMES NOT: A PRIEST AND IT IS IN A GRAVEYARD; AN ELDER AND IT IS BENEATH HIS DIGNITY; HIS OWN LOSS GREATER THAN HIS FELLOW\'S — EXEMPT. ({SP_(222, 7, "היה", "כהן")} "he was a priest"; {SP_(222, 7, "לפי", "כבודו")} "according to his dignity"; {SP_(222, 7, "פטור")} "exempt"): THE THREE EXEMPTIONS read out of "hide yourself" — the priest\'s purity, the elder\'s honor, the finder\'s greater loss — the compile\'s exemption parameters (Bava Metzia 2:9 the answer sheet\'s ground). Fresh.')
srow(222, 8, 'MATERIAL', f'"SURELY RETURN THEM" — RETURNED AND IT FLED, RETURNED AND IT FLED, EVEN FIVE TIMES — LIABLE; RETURNED TO A PLACE WHERE OTHERS SAW IT — THEY NEED NOT TEND IT; STOLEN OR LOST — LIABLE FOR IT, ALWAYS, UNTIL HE BRINGS IT INTO HIS OWNER\'S DOMAIN. ({SP_(222, 8, "אפלו", "חמש", "פעמים", "חיב")} "even five times — liable"; {SP_(222, 8, "עד", "שיכניסנה", "לרשותו")} "until he brings it into his domain"): the doubled verb "surely return" the repetition\'s ground and the finder\'s LIABILITY STATUS until the owner\'s domain (Bava Metzia 2:9; Tosefta 2:23) — the compile\'s status on the finder. Fresh.')
srow(223, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"IF YOUR BROTHER IS NOT NEAR" (22:2) — ONLY NEAR? FAR FROM "AND YOU KNOW HIM NOT". The head row of piska 223 ({SP_(223, 1, "רחוק", "מנין")} "far — whence?"): the distance no limit — the unknown owner the far one. Fresh.')
srow(223, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"GATHER IT INTO YOUR HOUSE" — AND NOT INTO ANOTHER HOUSE. ({SP_(223, 2, "ולא", "לבית", "אחר")} "and not to another house"): the finder\'s own keeping — no delegation. Fresh.')
srow(223, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"UNTIL YOUR BROTHER SEEKS IT" — WOULD YOU GIVE IT BEFORE HE GIVES ITS MARKS? WHY "UNTIL YOUR BROTHER SEEKS IT"? UNTIL YOU SEEK OUT YOUR BROTHER — WHETHER HE IS A FRAUD OR NOT. ({SP_(223, 3, "עד", "שלא", "יתן", "סימנים")} "before he gives marks"; {SP_(223, 3, "אם", "רמי", "הוא")} "whether he is a fraud"): THE MARKS (simanim) the claimant\'s proof and the finder\'s inquiry into the claimant — the return\'s two conditions (Bava Metzia 2:7 the answer sheet). Fresh.')
srow(223, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND RETURN IT TO HIM" — EVEN HIMSELF YOU RETURN TO HIM. ({SP_(223, 4, "אף", "את", "עצמו", "אתה", "משיב", "לו")} "even himself you return to him"): THE LOST MAN — the duty widened from the beast to the wanderer guided home (Tosefta Bava Metzia 2:28, not opened); a find of the reading. Fresh.')
srow(224, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"SO SHALL YOU DO WITH HIS ASS" (22:3) — AN ASS: IT WORKS AND EATS. The head row of piska 224 ({SP_(224, 1, "עושה", "ואוכלת")} "it works and eats"): the kept beast\'s upkeep from its labor (Bava Metzia 2:7) — the compile\'s parameter on the keeping. Fresh.')
srow(224, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'A GARMENT — HE SHAKES IT ONCE IN THIRTY DAYS; SPREADS IT FOR ITS OWN NEED, NOT FOR HIS HONOR. ({SP_(224, 2, "אחת", "לשלשים", "יום")} "once in thirty days"): A CLOCK PARAMETER on the kept garment\'s care (Bava Metzia 2:8 the answer sheet) — the keeping\'s calendar. Fresh.')
srow(224, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'VESSELS OF SILVER AND OF COPPER — HE USES THEM FOR THEIR OWN NEED, NOT TO WEAR THEM OUT. ({SP_(224, 3, "אבל", "לא", "לשחקם")} "but not to wear them out"): the use bounded by the object\'s good. Fresh.')
srow(224, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'VESSELS OF WOOD — HE USES THEM SO THEY DO NOT ROT (BAVA METZIA 2:8). ({SP_(224, 4, "כדי", "שלא", "ירקבו")} "so that they do not rot"): the third material — the keeping by kind. Fresh.')
srow(224, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'THE GARMENT WAS IN THE CLASS OF ALL THESE — WHY SINGLED OUT? TO COMPARE TO IT: AS A GARMENT HAS MARKS AND CLAIMANTS, SO EVERYTHING WITH MARKS AND CLAIMANTS; ONLY THESE? "EVERY LOST THING OF YOUR BROTHER". ({SP_(224, 5, "להקיש", "אליה")} "to compare to it"; {SP_(224, 5, "סימנים", "ויש", "לה", "תובעים")} "marks and it has claimants"): THE CLASS DEFINED BY THE PROTOTYPE — marks and claimants the two properties of returnable property (I3 the prototype), "every lost thing" the widening (Bava Metzia 2:8\'s list). Fresh.')
srow(224, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'"WHICH IS LOST FROM HIM" — EXCLUDING LESS THAN A PERUTAH\'S WORTH; R. JUDAH SAYS: "AND YOU FOUND IT" — INCLUDING LESS THAN A PERUTAH. ({SP_(224, 6, "פרט", "לפחות", "משוה", "פרוטה")} "excluding less than a perutah\'s worth"): THE THRESHOLD PARAMETER of the duty — a perutah (the smallest coin) — with R. Judah\'s dissent, a disputed cell. Fresh.')
srow(224, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'"YOU MAY NOT HIDE YOURSELF" — TO SET IT UNDER A NEGATIVE COMMANDMENT. ({SP_(224, 7, "בלא", "תעשה")} "under a negative commandment"): 22:3\'s close the prohibition\'s seat for every kind of lost thing. Fresh.')
srow(225, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"YOU SHALL NOT SEE" (22:4) — A NEGATIVE COMMANDMENT; ELSEWHERE "WHEN YOU SEE" (Exodus 23:5) — A POSITIVE ONE. The head row of piska 225 ({SP_(225, 1, "מצות", "עשה")} "a positive commandment"): the fallen ass\'s pair as the lost ox\'s (222:4) — the two books one law in two forms. Fresh.')
srow(225, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"YOUR BROTHER\'S ASS" — ONLY YOUR BROTHER\'S? YOUR HATER\'S FROM "YOUR HATER\'S ASS" (Exodus 23:5) — ANY OWNER; WHY "BROTHER"? THE TORAH SPEAKS ONLY AGAINST THE INCLINATION. ({SP_(225, 2, "חמור", "שונאך", "מנין")} "your hater\'s ass — whence?"): 222:5\'s words for the fallen beast — the scope every owner. Fresh.')
srow(225, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"FALLEN" — AND NOT STANDING. ({SP_(225, 3, "ולא", "עומדים")} "and not standing"): the duty\'s condition the beast down. Fresh.')
srow(225, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"ON THE WAY" — AND NOT IN THE STABLE; HENCE (BAVA METZIA 2:10): FOUND IT IN THE STABLE — NO DUTY; IN THE PUBLIC DOMAIN — THE DUTY. THE MISHNAH CITED IN THE HEBREW BY NAME ({SP_(225, 4, "ולא", "ברפת")} "and not in the stable"; {SP_(225, 4, "ברשות", "הרבים", "חיב", "בה")} "in the public domain — liable for it"): THE PLACE PARAMETER — the way and the public domain against the stable. Fresh.')
srow(225, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOU HIDE YOURSELF" — SOMETIMES YOU HIDE AND SOMETIMES NOT: THE PRIEST IN THE GRAVEYARD, THE ELDER\'S DIGNITY, THE GREATER LOSS — EXEMPT. ({SP_(225, 5, "פטור")} "exempt"): 222:7\'s three exemptions repeated for the fallen beast — one exemption table for the two laws. Fresh.')
srow(225, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'"RAISE WITH HIM" — RAISED AND IT FELL, EVEN FIVE TIMES — LIABLE; THE OWNER WENT AND SAT AND SAID "SINCE THE COMMANDMENT IS ON YOU, RAISE IT IF YOU WISH" — EXEMPT, FOR IT SAYS "WITH HIM"; EVEN AN ELDER, A SICK MAN, ONE SMITTEN WITH BOILS? "WITH HIM". ({SP_(225, 6, "הואיל", "ועליך", "מצוה")} "since the commandment is on you"; {SP_(225, 6, "ואפלו", "מכה", "שחין")} "and even one smitten with boils"): THE OWNER\'S PART A CONDITION — "with him" exempts the helper when the owner sits down, and binds even the infirm (Bava Metzia 2:10 the answer sheet); the compile\'s two arms. Fresh.')
srow(226, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"NO MAN\'S GEAR ON A WOMAN" (22:5) — WHAT DOES THE VERSE TEACH, THAT A WOMAN NOT WEAR WHITE GARMENTS NOR A MAN COLORED ONES? "ABOMINATION" — A THING THAT LEADS TO ABOMINATION; THE RULE: A WOMAN NOT DRESS AS A MAN AND GO AMONG MEN, A MAN NOT ADORN HIMSELF WITH WOMEN\'S ORNAMENTS AND GO AMONG WOMEN. The head row of piska 226 ({SP_(226, 1, "דבר", "הבא", "לידי", "תועבה")} "a thing that comes to abomination"; {SP_(226, 1, "ותלך", "לבין", "האנשים")} "and go among the men"): THE PRINCIPLE — the garment\'s law read by its purpose (mixing among the other sex), not by color; the compile\'s predicate on the act. Fresh.')
srow(226, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'R. ELIEZER B. JACOB SAYS: WHENCE THAT A WOMAN NOT WEAR WEAPONS AND GO OUT TO WAR? "NO MAN\'S GEAR ON A WOMAN"; THAT A MAN NOT ADORN HIMSELF WITH WOMEN\'S ORNAMENTS? "A MAN SHALL NOT WEAR A WOMAN\'S GARMENT". ({SP_(226, 2, "כלי", "זין", "ותצא", "למלחמה")} "weapons, and go out to war"): ONKELOS\'S RENDERING IS R. ELIEZER B. JACOB\'S — "the armament of a man" (the ink\'s find 15): the Aramaic writes this row\'s reading into the verse; the war daemon\'s exemption of women a status. Fresh.')
srow(226, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"FOR AN ABOMINATION OF THE LORD YOUR GOD IS EVERYONE WHO DOES THESE" — HE IS CALLED BY FIVE NAMES: CONDEMNED, ABOMINATION, HATED, DETESTABLE AND PERVERSE (SIFRA, KEDOSHIM). ({SP_(226, 3, "קרוי", "חמשה", "שמות")} "called by five names"): THE FIVE EPITHETS of the abomination formula\'s subject — the sanction\'s vocabulary at the formula\'s fifth seat of eight (the ink\'s find 5); 25:16\'s "all who do these" the twin run. Fresh.')
